{
  "about": "Every place that shows the glucose card or its value, per platform: THE registry behind 'One graph everywhere' (CLAUDE.md) and the freshness steps. A 'card' surface draws card pixels only through the renderer (GlucoseCard.draw / GlucoseCard.image) and chooses only its size, its place's settings and the parts; a 'glyph' surface (text, icons and words the system lays out) takes the value, the trend mark and the freshness steps from GlucoseCard.face (a GlucoseLook) and never formats a glucose value itself. tools/check: card-surface (a file that calls the renderer must be a registered file of the surface it names; every surface is rendered by the tests), card-api (outside 'owners' only the 'api' members of the renderer's namespaces: every painter, found automatically, and the 'api' keys), card-text (no surface formats a glucose value itself; '// card-ok: <why>' marks a line that must). CardLayoutTest (Android) and -graphselftest (Mac) render ../layout/scenes.json through each surface's real entry path at its sizes and check ../layout/rules.json; FreshnessFixtureTest and -graphselftest run the card and every glyph surface through ../freshness/freshness.json's steps. Sizes are dp / pt of the surface's own box (see each surface's 'size'). A card surface draws its value through the renderer too (one of the parts all / header / value) unless its entry has 'no_value' with the reason (CardLayoutTest, -graphselftest). Paths are the V1 apps' (apps/android, apps/macos); 'owners', 'sources' and 'tests' are globs. A named file that doesn't exist yet is a 'pending V1 file' NOTE until tools/check/v1-complete exists; the chunk that writes a surface moves its entry to its real file.",
